    <p class="sidebar-card bg-[#371600] mt-6 max-w-[99vw] mb-2">
        Every game listed in this page have same working mechanism. Same requirement, and you can play them alone as well. <br>
        Game ends when you reach the score target or when someone uses the <code>/endgame</code> command.
    </p>

    <div>
        <section id="anime" class="game-card rounded-3xl overflow-hidden bg-[#371600] border border-[var(--sayori-border)]">
            <header class="card-header px-8 py-12">
                <div class="card-symbol">
                    💖
                </div>
                <h2 class="text-2xl text-[var(--sayori-lavender-bright)]">Anime Tea</h2>
                <p class="card-tagline">
                    Think you know about your favourite anime. Take a short quiz.
                </p>
            </header>
            <div class="px-8 pb-8 space-y-10">
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold mb-4">🎮 How to Play</h3>
                    <p class="text-[var(--sayori-muted)] leading-8">
                        Sayori will send a question in the chat. The first one to send the right answer gets the point. <br>If no one answers for 7 consecutive questions, them the game ends on it's own.
                    </p>
                </section>
                <section>

                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Anime Lists</h3>
                    <p class="text-[var(--sayori-muted)] mt-5 leading-8">
                        If you want to play a specific Anime.
                    </p>

                    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                        <span class="game-chip">🧟‍♀️ Attack on titan</span>
                        <span class="game-chip">🔗 Chainsaw Man</span>
                        <span class="game-chip">🍎 Deathnote</span>
                        <span class="game-chip">🧟‍♀️ Demon Slayer</span>
                        <span class="game-chip">🔗 Jujutsu Kaisen</span>
                        <span class="game-chip">🍎 My hero Academia</span>
                        <span class="game-chip">🥷🏾 Naruto</span>
                        <span class="game-chip">🏴‍☠️ One piece</span>
                        <span class="game-chip">🕵🏾‍♂️ SpyxFamily</span>
                    </div>

                    <p class="text-[var(--sayori-muted)] mt-5 leading-8">
                        write the name of the anime, you want to play in <code>anime_name</code> option to have only
                        that anime in the play.
                    </p>
                </section>
                <section>

                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold mb-4">⌨ Commands</h3>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                        <button class="copy-command p-2 rounded" data-command="/animetea">
                            /animetea
                        </button>
                        <button class="copy-command p-2 rounded" data-command="/endgame">
                            /endgame
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </section>
                <section>
                    <h3 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-semibold">How to use the commands?</h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-[var(--sayori-muted)]">
                        <li>type <code>/animetea anime_name: &lt;anime name&gt; pts: &lt;number&gt;</code> to start the
                            quiz only of your favourite anime.</li>
                        <li>To check the scores: <code>/animetea status</code></li>
                        <li>To have more that one anime, you can use the prefix command
                            <code>!animetea start anime1,anime2,...</code>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </section>
            </div>
        </section>
